calloop requests tracing's `log` feature unconditionally. In a workspace build that feature is unified into every
crate's `tracing`, whose macros then expand with the subscriber-free `log` fallback, and clippy's cognitive_complexity
counts those generated branches (about 10 per call site): 29 functions of the existing crates went over the limit
when ngterm-gpui brought GPUI (and calloop) in. Without the feature the graph is configured as it was before;
ngterm's subscriber is installed first thing in main, and `log` records still reach it through tracing-subscriber's
LogTracer bridge. scripts/vendor-calloop.sh applies this to the verified crates.io archive.

--- a/Cargo.toml
+++ b/Cargo.toml
@@ -114,7 +114,7 @@

 [dependencies.tracing]
 version = "0.1.40"
-features = ["log"]
+features = []
 default-features = false

 [dev-dependencies.criterion]
